<access component="com_alfa">
	<section name="component">
		<!--
			Joomla's own two component rights: Configure (Options and this Permissions tab) and
			Access Administration Interface (entering Alfa at all). Joomla checks both itself:
			com_config, the component dispatcher and the admin menu, so they stay.

			Everything else is Alfa's: each screen has its own view / create / edit / change
			state / delete, checked through AlfaHelper::can(), and only the ones something
			checks. The append-only movements ledger offers View alone. Carts offer Edit only to
			take over a cart a storefront shopper created, asked together with Check out on
			behalf and with Carts: View.
			Joomla's Create, Delete, Edit, Edit State and Edit Own are not used anywhere in Alfa
			and are not offered.

			Nothing is granted at install: a Super User can do everything, every other group only
			what a Super User grants here. Sections follow the admin menu, Tools last; plugin
			permissions are placed next to their own menu entry (AlfarulesField).
		-->
		<action name="core.admin" title="JACTION_ADMIN" description="JACTION_ADMIN" />
		<action name="core.manage" title="JACTION_MANAGE" description="JACTION_MANAGE" />

